counterfactuals.output:
1. **A system for comparing performance of a human operator with performance of a virtual clone, the system comprising:**  

   a controlled platform configured to receive control inputs from the human operator and to generate platform-state data and operator-performance data during performance of a task;  

   a sensing interface configured to acquire the platform-state data and the operator-performance data;  

   a memory storing a predetermined operator profile specifying virtual-clone control behavior for performing the task; and  

   one or more processors operatively coupled to the controlled platform, the sensing interface, and the memory, the one or more processors configured to:  

   cause a virtual representation of the controlled platform to perform a simulated instance of the task under control of a virtual clone operated according to the predetermined operator profile;  

   determine, from the simulated instance, virtual-clone performance data corresponding to the operator-performance data;  

   compare the operator-performance data with the virtual-clone performance data under a common set of task conditions;  

   generate at least one comparative performance metric based on the comparison; and  

   provide an output indicative of a difference between performance of the human operator and performance of the virtual clone.
